WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.378
Building an agent is easy. Trusting it is hard.

00:00:04.478 --> 00:00:09.764
Roughly eighty percent of the effort goes into infrastructure, security, and validation.

00:00:10.964 --> 00:00:18.762
Put one gateway in front of every model call. Masking. Caching. Retries and failover.

00:00:18.812 --> 00:00:19.898
Token accounting.

00:00:20.448 --> 00:00:26.526
Then trace every run. Token counts per call. The tool call sequence.

00:00:26.576 --> 00:00:27.630
And who triggered it.

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:33.106
The dangerous input is not what the user types. It is what comes back.

00:00:33.656 --> 00:00:40.232
Change rides one rail: evals gate the merge, canary rollout, watch the traces,

00:00:40.282 --> 00:00:41.678
roll back instantly.

00:00:42.228 --> 00:00:49.015
Day one, one cheap move per layer. Context: keep the stable part byte stable.

00:00:49.065 --> 00:00:55.395
Loop: a turn limit and a dollar limit. Gate: label two hundred examples.

00:00:55.445 --> 00:00:58.881
Harness: a user that cannot delete anything.

00:00:58.931 --> 00:01:02.082
Evals: write the last five failures down.

00:01:02.632 --> 00:01:08.566
That's module six, production. Start with page one: From Prototype to Production.
